  "editorial": "sorted is ascending. A descending score is an ascending negated score. The name stays unnegated so ties go from a to z. One key keeps the two directions from fighting across two sorts.",
  "reference_solution": "def solve(rows):\n    ordered = sorted(rows, key=lambda row: (-row[1], row[0]))\n    return [list(row) for row in ordered]\n"
}
